									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3460794&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608840126" alt="Kothardarastrix" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3460794)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;" >Kothardarastrix</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608832698 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Dec 2020 17:58</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-88827/foundation-universe">SCP Universe / Foundation Universe</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13941623/what-award-would-somebody-get-for-neutralizing-a-keter">What award would somebody get for neutralizing a keter?</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852844">
									

<p>Nothing. If this dude can neutralize 106 or some other impossible to destroy, nearly impossible to contain anomaly he could also flatten site 19 or eradicate the O5 council from existence, or make himself the supreme God emperor of earth or something. Reality benders are too powerful and too unpredictable for a control-freak organization like the Foundation to tolerate, no matter how cooperative they are, because they might become uncooperative in the future. That’s why most of the free-willed reality benders with full control of their powers in the SCP verse have either been decommissioned by Clef or liquidated by the GOC. If your character destroyed 106, the foundation would send Dr. Clef to kill him or otherwise make sure he doesn’t get the chance to destroy anything else.</p>
<p>Also, don’t make a superhero character and beat up 682. That’s a Mary Sue and the Worf Effect. Anomalous people, regardless of how helpful they ostensibly are, are monsters at worse and the victims of a terrible condition at best. If it has powers that you would like to have, it’s not an SCP. As a general rule, anyway.</p>

							</div>

								
					
